#Problem APEX 6.1.24

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Techniques of integration)
## DBsection(Substitution (without trigonometric functions))
## KEYWORDS('indefinite integral')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('6.1')
## Problem1('24')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',                'PGML.pl',
    'parserFormulaUpToConstant.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

## (a) ##
$a1 = random(2, 9, 1);
$b1 = non_zero_random(-9, 9, 1);

$u1 = "$a1 x + $b1";

$f1 = "e^{$u1}";

#### Answers ####

$F1 = FormulaUpToConstant("e^{$u1} / $a1");

BEGIN_PGML
Evaluate the indefinite integral using substitution. (Use [`C`]
for the constant of integration.)

[``  \int [$f1] \, dx = \;``][_]{$F1}{40}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Substitute [`u = [$u1]`].  Then [`du = [$a1] \,dx`].

[```
  \begin{aligned}
      \int [$f1] \, dx& =
     \dfrac{1}{[$a1]} \int e^u \, du \\
   & = \dfrac{1}{[$a1]} e^u + C\\
   & = \dfrac{1}{[$a1]} e^{[$u1]} + C. \\
  \end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();

